# deploiement/config/flags.map
#
# One-to-one mapping between the 12 vulnerable services and the flag_id
# column of enonce/flags-G04.csv. Format: SERVICE_REF=flag_id, one mapping
# per line. Read exactly by flag_id via lib/common.sh:mv_flag_value — flag
# values are never duplicated here or anywhere else in the repo.
#
# Order: the three N1 entry points first, in ARCHITECTURE.md's listed order
# (E2, E3, E5), then each chain's pivots in the exact discovery order
# ARCHITECTURE.md describes (flag discovery follows attack-chain
# progression):
#   Chain A: E2 leaks the route -> E7 reveals E8 -> E8 reveals the
#            PostgreSQL account -> E10 holds the final flag.
#   Chain B: E5 reveals the Jenkins path -> E14 reveals E12 -> E12 reveals
#            the mongo-express account -> E11 holds the clients flag.
#   Chain C: E3 reveals E6 -> E6 reveals the E9 share -> E9 holds the WMS
#            procedure -> E13 holds the logistics flag.

E2=1
E3=2
E5=3
E7=4
E8=5
E10=6
E14=7
E12=8
E11=9
E6=10
E9=11
E13=12
